-- The Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238: definitions, application and
-- the other rules of the Act that a computer can answer. The rules that count time are in
-- `bc-interpretation-time.l4`; the rules on repeal are in `bc-interpretation-repeal.l4`.
--
-- Draft. A single Sonnet 5.5 agent wrote this from the text alone; no domain expert has read it
-- against the statute. The quotations are copied from `RSBC-1996-c.-238.txt`, a plain-text
-- rendering made by a script (not the official text), by `srcrefs.py`; `src:N` is line N of that file.
--
-- Where a rule of the Act is a canon of construction with no condition to compute (for example
-- that words in the singular include the plural, s 28(3)), it is not forced into code; the
-- coverage table in NOTES.md says so, with the reason.
--
-- Target compiler: `unstable` (REFUSE and YMD are rejected by `main`).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `s 1 Definitions`

-- The plain-text rendering prints paragraphs (a) and (b) of "regulation" AFTER the semicolon
-- that ends the definition (src:14-16). On its face they qualify "enacted"; this encoding reads
-- them so (see NOTES, fork F-rendering-order). The rendering is not the official text, so the
-- official order of words may differ.
-- src:14 | regulation means a regulation, order, rule, form, tariff of costs or fees, proclamation, letters patent, commission, warrant, bylaw or other instrument enacted but does not include an order of a court made in the course of an action or an order made by a public officer or administrative tribunal in a dispute between 2 or more persons;
-- src:15 | (a) in execution of a power conferred under an Act, or
-- src:16 | (b) by or under the authority of the Lieutenant Governor in Council,
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 1 "regulation" (src:14-16)
GIVEN listedKind    IS A BOOLEAN   -- a regulation, order, rule, form, tariff of costs or fees, proclamation, letters patent, commission, warrant, bylaw or other instrument
      underAnAct    IS A BOOLEAN   -- enacted in execution of a power conferred under an Act
      byTheLGinC    IS A BOOLEAN   -- enacted by or under the authority of the Lieutenant Governor in Council
      courtOrder    IS A BOOLEAN   -- an order of a court made in the course of an action
      disputeOrder  IS A BOOLEAN   -- an order made by a public officer or administrative tribunal in a dispute between 2 or more persons
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 an instrument is a regulation` listedKind underAnAct byTheLGinC courtOrder disputeOrder MEANS
        listedKind
    AND (underAnAct OR byTheLGinC)
    AND NOT (courtOrder OR disputeOrder)

-- src:12 | enactment means an Act or a regulation or a portion of an Act or regulation;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 1 "enactment" (src:12)
GIVEN isAnAct       IS A BOOLEAN
      isARegulation IS A BOOLEAN
      isAPortion    IS A BOOLEAN   -- a portion of an Act or regulation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 a thing is an enactment` isAnAct isARegulation isAPortion MEANS
    isAnAct OR isARegulation OR isAPortion

§ `s 2 Application`

-- src:20 | 2 (1) Every provision of this Act applies to every enactment, whether enacted before or after the commencement of this Act, unless a contrary intention appears in this Act or in the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 2(1) (src:20)
GIVEN contraryIntentionInThisAct   IS A BOOLEAN
      contraryIntentionInEnactment IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` contraryIntentionInThisAct contraryIntentionInEnactment MEANS
    NOT (contraryIntentionInThisAct OR contraryIntentionInEnactment)

§ `s 5 Preliminary proceedings`

-- Before the enactment is in force, a thing done under a power to make it effective "has no
-- effect until the enactment comes into force, except insofar as is necessary to make the
-- enactment effective on its coming into force". The extent of "insofar as necessary" is a
-- question of fact for the caller; this answers only whether the thing has any effect on a day.
-- src:41 | 5 (1) If an enactment that is not in force contains provisions conferring power to make regulations, or to do any other thing, to make the enactment effective on its coming into force, the power may be exercised before the enactment comes into force, but the regulation or the thing done has no effect until the enactment comes into force, except insofar as is necessary to make the enactment effective on its coming into force.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 5(1) (src:41)
GIVEN `the day the enactment comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day in question`                    IS A DATE
      `to the extent necessary to make the enactment effective on its coming into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(1) a thing done before commencement has effect on a day` `the day the enactment comes into force` `the day in question` `to the extent necessary to make the enactment effective on its coming into force` MEANS
        `the day in question` AT LEAST `the day the enactment comes into force`
    OR  `to the extent necessary to make the enactment effective on its coming into force`

§ `s 14 Government bound by enactments`

-- src:84 | 14 (1) Unless it specifically provides otherwise, an enactment is binding on the government.
-- src:85 | (2) Despite subsection (1), an enactment that would bind or affect the government in the use or development of land, or in the planning, construction, alteration, servicing, maintenance or use of improvements, as defined in the Assessment Act, does not bind or affect the government.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 14(1) and (2) (src:84-85)
GIVEN specificallyProvidesItDoesNotBind IS A BOOLEAN
      affectsGovernmentInLandUse        IS A BOOLEAN   -- would bind or affect the government in the use or development of land, or in the planning, construction, alteration, servicing, maintenance or use of improvements, as defined in the Assessment Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14 an enactment binds the government` specificallyProvidesItDoesNotBind affectsGovernmentInLandUse MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF affectsGovernmentInLandUse THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOT specificallyProvidesItDoesNotBind

§ `s 18 Majority and quorum`

-- src:108 | 18 (1) If in an enactment an act or thing is required or authorized to be done by more than 2 persons, a majority of them may do it.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(1) (src:108)
GIVEN `the number of persons by whom the act is required or authorized to be done` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those persons who do it`                                      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) a majority of the persons may do the act` `the number of persons by whom the act is required or authorized to be done` `the number of those persons who do it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of persons by whom the act is required or authorized to be done` AT MOST 2
            THEN `s 18(1) applies only where more than 2 persons are to do the act`
        IF `the number of those persons who do it` ABOVE (`the number of persons by whom the act is required or authorized to be done` DIVIDED BY 2)
            THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `s 18(1) says what a majority of them may do and does not say what fewer may do`

-- src:108 | 18 (1) If in an enactment an act or thing is required or authorized to be done by more than 2 persons, a majority of them may do it.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(1) (src:108)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) applies only where more than 2 persons are to do the act` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 18(1) applies only where more than 2 persons are to do the act"

-- src:108 | 18 (1) If in an enactment an act or thing is required or authorized to be done by more than 2 persons, a majority of them may do it.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(1) (src:108)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) says what a majority of them may do and does not say what fewer may do` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 18(1) says what a majority of them may do and does not say what fewer may do"

-- src:109 | (2) If an enactment establishes a board, commission or other body consisting of 3 or more members, in this subsection called the "association", the following rules apply:
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(2) (src:109)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(2) applies only to a body of 3 or more members` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 18(2) applies only to a body of 3 or more members"

-- src:111 | (b) if the number of members of the association provided for by the enactment is not a fixed number, at least 1/2 of the number of members in office constitutes a quorum at a meeting of the association, as long as the number of members is within the maximum or minimum number, if any, authorized by the enactment;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(2)(b) (src:111)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(2)(b) does not say what constitutes a quorum when the number of members is outside the authorized maximum or minimum` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 18(2)(b) does not say what constitutes a quorum when the number of members is outside the authorized maximum or minimum"

-- The threshold of "at least 1/2": one half of the fixed number (para (a)) or of the number of members
-- in office (para (b)). It can be a fraction: for 7 members it is 3.5. The whole number of members that
-- a client counts is the next function, which rounds the threshold up.
-- src:109 | (2) If an enactment establishes a board, commission or other body consisting of 3 or more members, in this subsection called the "association", the following rules apply:
-- src:110 | (a) if the number of members of the association provided for by the enactment is a fixed number, at least 1/2 of that number of members constitutes a quorum at a meeting of the association;
-- src:111 | (b) if the number of members of the association provided for by the enactment is not a fixed number, at least 1/2 of the number of members in office constitutes a quorum at a meeting of the association, as long as the number of members is within the maximum or minimum number, if any, authorized by the enactment;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(2)(a) and (b) (src:109-111)
GIVEN `the number of members provided for by the enactment` IS A NUMBER
      `that number is a fixed number`                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members in office`                     IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members is within the authorized maximum or minimum, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(2) the threshold of one half, before it is rounded up to a whole number of members` `the number of members provided for by the enactment` `that number is a fixed number` `the number of members in office` `the number of members is within the authorized maximum or minimum, if any` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of members provided for by the enactment` BELOW 3
            THEN `s 18(2) applies only to a body of 3 or more members`
        IF `that number is a fixed number`
            THEN `the number of members provided for by the enactment` DIVIDED BY 2
        IF `the number of members is within the authorized maximum or minimum, if any`
            THEN `the number of members in office` DIVIDED BY 2
        OTHERWISE `s 18(2)(b) does not say what constitutes a quorum when the number of members is outside the authorized maximum or minimum`

-- The number of members that must be present to constitute a quorum: the smallest WHOLE number of members
-- that reaches "at least 1/2" of the fixed number (para (a)) or of the number in office (para (b)).
-- For 5 fixed members it is 3, for 3 fixed members 2, for 7 in office 4; for 10 fixed members it is 5.
-- src:109 | (2) If an enactment establishes a board, commission or other body consisting of 3 or more members, in this subsection called the "association", the following rules apply:
-- src:110 | (a) if the number of members of the association provided for by the enactment is a fixed number, at least 1/2 of that number of members constitutes a quorum at a meeting of the association;
-- src:111 | (b) if the number of members of the association provided for by the enactment is not a fixed number, at least 1/2 of the number of members in office constitutes a quorum at a meeting of the association, as long as the number of members is within the maximum or minimum number, if any, authorized by the enactment;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(2)(a) and (b) (src:109-111)
GIVEN `the number of members provided for by the enactment` IS A NUMBER
      `that number is a fixed number`                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members in office`                     IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members is within the authorized maximum or minimum, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(2) the number the members present must reach to constitute a quorum` `the number of members provided for by the enactment` `that number is a fixed number` `the number of members in office` `the number of members is within the authorized maximum or minimum, if any` MEANS
    CEILING (`s 18(2) the threshold of one half, before it is rounded up to a whole number of members` `the number of members provided for by the enactment` `that number is a fixed number` `the number of members in office` `the number of members is within the authorized maximum or minimum, if any`)

-- src:112 | (c) an act or thing done by a majority of the members of the association present at a meeting, if the members present constitute a quorum, is deemed to have been done by the association;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(2)(c) (src:112)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(2)(c) speaks only of an act or thing done at a meeting at which the members present constitute a quorum` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 18(2)(c) speaks only of an act or thing done at a meeting at which the members present constitute a quorum"

-- src:112 | (c) an act or thing done by a majority of the members of the association present at a meeting, if the members present constitute a quorum, is deemed to have been done by the association;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(2)(c) (src:112)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(2)(c) says what a majority of the members present may do and does not say what fewer may do` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 18(2)(c) says what a majority of the members present may do and does not say what fewer may do"

-- src:112 | (c) an act or thing done by a majority of the members of the association present at a meeting, if the members present constitute a quorum, is deemed to have been done by the association;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(2)(c) (src:112)
GIVEN `the number of members present at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the number the members present must reach to constitute a quorum` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the members present who do the act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(2)(c) the act is deemed to have been done by the association` `the number of members present at the meeting` `the number the members present must reach to constitute a quorum` `the number of the members present who do the act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of members present at the meeting` BELOW `the number the members present must reach to constitute a quorum`
            THEN `s 18(2)(c) speaks only of an act or thing done at a meeting at which the members present constitute a quorum`
        IF `the number of the members present who do the act` ABOVE (`the number of members present at the meeting` DIVIDED BY 2)
            THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `s 18(2)(c) says what a majority of the members present may do and does not say what fewer may do`

-- src:113 | (d) a vacancy in the membership of the association does not invalidate the constitution of the association or impair the right of the members in office to act, if the number of members in office is not less than a quorum.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(2)(d) (src:113)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(2)(d) speaks only of a vacancy where the number of members in office is not less than a quorum` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 18(2)(d) speaks only of a vacancy where the number of members in office is not less than a quorum"

-- src:113 | (d) a vacancy in the membership of the association does not invalidate the constitution of the association or impair the right of the members in office to act, if the number of members in office is not less than a quorum.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 18(2)(d) (src:113)
GIVEN `the number of members in office` IS A NUMBER
      `the number the members present must reach to constitute a quorum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(2)(d) a vacancy does not impair the right of the members in office to act` `the number of members in office` `the number the members present must reach to constitute a quorum` MEANS
    IF   `the number of members in office` AT LEAST `the number the members present must reach to constitute a quorum`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 18(2)(d) speaks only of a vacancy where the number of members in office is not less than a quorum`

§ `s 24 Documentary evidence`

-- src:151 | 24 If an enactment provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact, unless the context indicates that the document is conclusive evidence, the document is admissible in evidence in any proceeding, and the fact is deemed to be established in the absence of any evidence to the contrary.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 24 (src:151)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24 speaks only of an enactment that provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 24 speaks only of an enactment that provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact"

-- src:151 | 24 If an enactment provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact, unless the context indicates that the document is conclusive evidence, the document is admissible in evidence in any proceeding, and the fact is deemed to be established in the absence of any evidence to the contrary.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 24 (src:151)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24 does not say what follows where the context indicates the document is conclusive evidence` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 24 does not say what follows where the context indicates the document is conclusive evidence"

-- src:151 | 24 If an enactment provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact, unless the context indicates that the document is conclusive evidence, the document is admissible in evidence in any proceeding, and the fact is deemed to be established in the absence of any evidence to the contrary.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 24 (src:151)
GIVEN providesDocumentIsEvidence IS A BOOLEAN
      contextIndicatesConclusive IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24 the document is admissible in evidence in any proceeding` providesDocumentIsEvidence contextIndicatesConclusive MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT providesDocumentIsEvidence THEN `s 24 speaks only of an enactment that provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact`
        IF contextIndicatesConclusive THEN `s 24 does not say what follows where the context indicates the document is conclusive evidence`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:151 | 24 If an enactment provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact, unless the context indicates that the document is conclusive evidence, the document is admissible in evidence in any proceeding, and the fact is deemed to be established in the absence of any evidence to the contrary.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 24 (src:151)
GIVEN providesDocumentIsEvidence IS A BOOLEAN
      contextIndicatesConclusive IS A BOOLEAN
      thereIsEvidenceToTheContrary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24 the fact is deemed to be established` providesDocumentIsEvidence contextIndicatesConclusive thereIsEvidenceToTheContrary MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT providesDocumentIsEvidence THEN `s 24 speaks only of an enactment that provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact`
        IF contextIndicatesConclusive THEN `s 24 does not say what follows where the context indicates the document is conclusive evidence`
        OTHERWISE NOT thereIsEvidenceToTheContrary

§ `s 28 Use of forms`

-- src:216 | 28 (1) If a form is prescribed under an enactment, deviations from it not affecting the substance or calculated to mislead, do not invalidate the form used.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 28(1) (src:216)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) speaks only of a form prescribed under an enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 28(1) speaks only of a form prescribed under an enactment"

-- src:216 | 28 (1) If a form is prescribed under an enactment, deviations from it not affecting the substance or calculated to mislead, do not invalidate the form used.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 28(1) (src:216)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) does not say what follows for a deviation that affects the substance or is calculated to mislead` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 28(1) does not say what follows for a deviation that affects the substance or is calculated to mislead"

-- src:216 | 28 (1) If a form is prescribed under an enactment, deviations from it not affecting the substance or calculated to mislead, do not invalidate the form used.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 28(1) (src:216)
GIVEN aFormIsPrescribed          IS A BOOLEAN
      deviationAffectsSubstance  IS A BOOLEAN
      deviationCalculatedToMislead IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) the deviation does not invalidate the form used` aFormIsPrescribed deviationAffectsSubstance deviationCalculatedToMislead MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT aFormIsPrescribed THEN `s 28(1) speaks only of a form prescribed under an enactment`
        IF deviationAffectsSubstance OR deviationCalculatedToMislead THEN `s 28(1) does not say what follows for a deviation that affects the substance or is calculated to mislead`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§ `s 29 Delivery, mail and minors`

-- "deliver ... includes mail to or leave with a person, or deposit in a person's mailbox or
-- receptacle at the person's residence or place of business". "mail" is the deposit in the
-- Canada Post Office at any place in Canada, postage prepaid. The Act says nothing about when a
-- mailed document is RECEIVED, and has no rule that deems it received after some days.
DECLARE `A way of delivering a notice or other document` IS ONE OF
    `Mailed to the person`
        HAS `the day it was deposited in the Canada Post Office`       IS A DATE
            `the place of deposit is in Canada`                        IS A BOOLEAN
            `postage was prepaid`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `Left with the person`
        HAS `the day it was left with the person`                      IS A DATE
    `Deposited in the person's mailbox or receptacle at the person's residence or place of business`
        HAS `the day it was deposited in the receptacle`               IS A DATE

-- src:269 | mail refers to the deposit of the matter to which the context applies in the Canada Post Office at any place in Canada, postage prepaid, for transmission by post, and includes deliver;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "mail" (src:269)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 29 does not make a deposit that is outside Canada or without prepaid postage a mailing` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 29 does not make a deposit that is outside Canada or without prepaid postage a mailing"

-- src:238 | deliver, with reference to a notice or other document, includes mail to or leave with a person, or deposit in a person's mailbox or receptacle at the person's residence or place of business;
-- src:269 | mail refers to the deposit of the matter to which the context applies in the Canada Post Office at any place in Canada, postage prepaid, for transmission by post, and includes deliver;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "deliver" and "mail" (src:238, src:269)
GIVEN way IS A `A way of delivering a notice or other document`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 29 the day a notice or other document is delivered` way MEANS
    CONSIDER way
        WHEN `Mailed to the person` deposited inCanada prepaid THEN
            IF inCanada AND prepaid
            THEN deposited
            ELSE `s 29 does not make a deposit that is outside Canada or without prepaid postage a mailing`
        WHEN `Left with the person` left THEN left
        WHEN `Deposited in the person's mailbox or receptacle at the person's residence or place of business` deposited THEN deposited

-- src:269 | mail refers to the deposit of the matter to which the context applies in the Canada Post Office at any place in Canada, postage prepaid, for transmission by post, and includes deliver;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "mail" (src:269)
GIVEN way IS A `A way of delivering a notice or other document`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 29 does not say when a mailed notice or other document is received` way MEANS
    REFUSE "s 29 does not say when a mailed notice or other document is received"

-- src:274 | minor means a person under the age of majority;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "minor" (src:274)
GIVEN age            IS A NUMBER
      `age of majority` IS A NUMBER   -- not stated in this Act: the caller supplies it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29 a person is a minor` age `age of majority` MEANS
    age BELOW `age of majority`

§ `s 33 References in enactments`

-- src:375 | 33 (1) A reference in an enactment to a series of numbers or letters by the first and last numbers or letters of the series includes the number or letter first and last mentioned.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 33(1) (src:375)
GIVEN first IS A NUMBER
      last  IS A NUMBER
      n     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(1) a number is in a series referred to by its first and last numbers` first last n MEANS
    first AT MOST n AND n AT MOST last

§ `s 38 Notice by newspaper`

-- src:410 | 38 If an enactment provides that notice must or may be given by publication in a newspaper published in a particular municipality, district, county, jurisdiction or other place, the provision must be construed to mean that the notice may be sufficiently given, if no newspaper is published at the time when the notice is to be given in the particular place, by publishing or advertising the notice in a newspaper published in British Columbia, nearest to the place mentioned.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 38 (src:410)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38 speaks only of a notice to be given where no newspaper is published in the particular place at the time` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 38 speaks only of a notice to be given where no newspaper is published in the particular place at the time"

-- src:410 | 38 If an enactment provides that notice must or may be given by publication in a newspaper published in a particular municipality, district, county, jurisdiction or other place, the provision must be construed to mean that the notice may be sufficiently given, if no newspaper is published at the time when the notice is to be given in the particular place, by publishing or advertising the notice in a newspaper published in British Columbia, nearest to the place mentioned.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 38 (src:410)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38 says that publication in the nearest British Columbia newspaper is sufficient and does not say that publication elsewhere is not` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 38 says that publication in the nearest British Columbia newspaper is sufficient and does not say that publication elsewhere is not"

-- src:410 | 38 If an enactment provides that notice must or may be given by publication in a newspaper published in a particular municipality, district, county, jurisdiction or other place, the provision must be construed to mean that the notice may be sufficiently given, if no newspaper is published at the time when the notice is to be given in the particular place, by publishing or advertising the notice in a newspaper published in British Columbia, nearest to the place mentioned.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 38 (src:410)
GIVEN `a newspaper is published in the particular place at the time the notice is to be given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is published in the British Columbia newspaper published nearest to the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38 publication in the nearest British Columbia newspaper makes the notice sufficiently given` `a newspaper is published in the particular place at the time the notice is to be given` `the notice is published in the British Columbia newspaper published nearest to the place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a newspaper is published in the particular place at the time the notice is to be given`
            THEN `s 38 speaks only of a notice to be given where no newspaper is published in the particular place at the time`
        IF NOT `the notice is published in the British Columbia newspaper published nearest to the place`
            THEN `s 38 says that publication in the nearest British Columbia newspaper is sufficient and does not say that publication elsewhere is not`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§ `s 42 Subdivisions of an Act`

DECLARE `Subdivision of a section` IS ONE OF
    Subsection
    Paragraph
    Subparagraph
    Clause

-- src:433 | (2) In an enactment enacted before July 1, 1974
-- src:434 | (a) a reference to a clause is deemed to be a reference to a paragraph,
-- src:435 | (b) a reference to a paragraph is deemed to be a reference to a subparagraph, and
-- src:436 | (c) a reference to a subparagraph is deemed to be a reference to a clause.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 42(2) (src:433-436)
GIVEN `the day the enactment was enacted`  IS A DATE
      `the subdivision the reference names` IS A `Subdivision of a section`
GIVETH A `Subdivision of a section`
`s 42(2) the subdivision a reference means` `the day the enactment was enacted` `the subdivision the reference names` MEANS
    IF   `the day the enactment was enacted` BELOW YMD 1974 7 1
    THEN CONSIDER `the subdivision the reference names`
             WHEN Clause        THEN Paragraph
             WHEN Paragraph     THEN Subparagraph
             WHEN Subparagraph  THEN Clause
             WHEN Subsection    THEN Subsection
    ELSE `the subdivision the reference names`
